1
00:00:00,466 --> 00:00:03,216
Why'd you set it
for the day before yesterday?

2
00:00:03,385 --> 00:00:06,925
Because I wanna go back and keep myself
from getting a time machine.

3
00:00:07,097 --> 00:00:10,437
(Sheldon:)You can't. If you were to prevent yourself
from buying it in the past...

4
00:00:10,601 --> 00:00:13,691
(Sheldon:)...you would not have it available
to stop yourself from buying it.

5
00:00:13,854 --> 00:00:18,064
(Sheldon:)Ergo, you would still have it.
This is a classic rookie time-travel mistake.

6
00:00:20,986 --> 00:00:24,156
(Leonard:)Can I go back and prevent you
from explaining that to me?

7
00:00:24,657 --> 00:00:25,697
(Sheldon:)Same paradox.

8
00:00:25,866 --> 00:00:28,746
(Sheldon:)If you were to travel back in time
and knock me unconscious...

9
00:00:28,911 --> 00:00:31,201
...you wouldn't have the conversation
that irritated you...

10
00:00:31,372 --> 00:00:34,002
(Sheldon:)...motivating you to go back
and knock me unconscious.

11
00:00:35,209 --> 00:00:37,669
(Leonard:)What if I knocked you unconscious
right now?

12
00:00:39,088 --> 00:00:41,258
(Sheldon:)It won't change the past.

13
00:00:42,591 --> 00:00:45,181
But it'd make the present so much nicer.

14
00:00:46,303 --> 00:00:48,643
(Sheldon:)Are you upset about something?

15
00:00:48,806 --> 00:00:50,766
(Leonard:)What was your first clue?

16
00:00:51,433 --> 00:00:54,313
(Sheldon:)Well, it was a number of things.
First, the late hour.

17
00:00:54,478 --> 00:00:56,358
Then your demeanor
seems very low-energy.

18
00:00:56,522 --> 00:00:58,352
(Sheldon:)- Plus your irritability...
- Yes, I'm upset.

19
00:00:58,524 --> 00:00:59,564
(Howard:)Oh.

20
00:00:59,733 --> 00:01:02,523
(Sheldon:)I don't usually pick up on those things.

